# Secondary review — slice 0160, postmortem 03

This is the owning orchestrator's advisory review of the agent-written
[primary postmortem](0160-03.postmortem-md). It is not an operator decision.
The only change authorized by this review is this report; no repair, commit,
acceptance, counter edit or relaunch was performed.

## Diagnosis

The immediate cause is a live configuration change: `.specrc.agent` changed
from `openai-codex` to `claude-code` after boot published the profile-1 receipt
and before the implementation worker returned. ASG fingerprints the entire
`.specrc` file, so the agent-selection change invalidated that receipt. The
post-worker guard escalated before build, elevation, tests or a new judge run.

I independently recomputed the receipt using the current ASG functions. The
only differing input is `inputs.specrc`. All source, bundle, prompt and validator
identities match, as do all 988 compiled descriptors and gate snapshots. The
stored `.specrc` identity matches committed HEAD; the working copy differs only
in the agent value after line-ending normalization. Product and elevation-driver
files have no diff against HEAD `37cb5491c313fe5a8ebe46c12c8a83435504c14b`.

The trigger is therefore configuration drift during execution. There is no
evidence of an implementation defect or recurrence of the arc-origin coverage
defect. ASG's current guard behaved according to its implementation, but its
generic error conceals the changed file and it couples backend selection to
proof validity. Those are tooling design/diagnostic concerns, separate from the
already-fixed schema and analyzer-scope incidents.

